      "hints": [
        "Evaluate $f'(4) = 6(\\frac{1}{2}) - 4(\\frac{1}{8}) = 2.5$.",
        "Multiply by $\\frac{dx}{dt} = 0.12$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Evaluate $f'(x) = 6x^{-1/2} - 4x^{-3/2}$ at $x = 4$:\n$$f'(4) = 6(4)^{-1/2} - 4(4)^{-3/2} = 6\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) - 4\\left(\\frac{1}{8}\\right) = 3 - 0.5 = 2.5 = \\frac{5}{2}$$",
        "Apply the chain rule $\\frac{dy}{dt} = \\frac{dy}{dx} \\times \\frac{dx}{dt}$ with $\\frac{dx}{dt} = 0.12\\text{ units s}^{-1}$:\n$$\\frac{dy}{dt} = \\frac{5}{2} \\times 0.12$$",
        "Calculate the rate of increase of the $y$-coordinate:\n$$\\frac{dy}{dt} = 0.3\\text{ units s}^{-1}$$"
      ],
